---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const emailCreators = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=Creator%20curation%20%E2%80%94%20tell%20us%20about%20your%20product";
const emailBroll = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=B-roll%20production%20%E2%80%94%20tell%20us%20about%20your%20product";
const emailGeneral = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=Creative%20testing%20%E2%80%94%20tell%20us%20about%20your%20product";
const calHref = "https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first";
---

<Layout
  title="Creative Testing — The Complete Guide | OKAD Agency"
  description="Everything about creative testing for paid ads: what it is, how it works, why most brands test wrong, and how to build a system that finds winners. An open reference by OKAD Agency."
>
  <Header />
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="pt-20 md:pt-24 pb-10 text-center bg-bg">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[12px] font-medium text-accent bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.18)] rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 mb-6">
          Open reference &middot; September 2026
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(28px,5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink mb-4">
          Creative Testing: <span class="text-accent">The Complete Guide</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-[18px] text-ink-2 max-w-[600px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-8">
          Creative testing is the practice of producing high volumes of ad variations and using real purchase data to find winners. This guide covers how it works, why most brands test wrong, and how to build a system that scales.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap mb-8">
          <a href={emailCreators} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-accent text-white hover:bg-accent-hover transition-all no-underline">Order creator curation &rarr;</a>
          <a href={emailBroll} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-card text-ink border border-border hover:border-accent hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Order B-roll production &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-5 flex-wrap justify-center font-mono text-[12px] text-muted">
          <span>Paid ads</span>
          <span>UGC</span>
          <span>B-roll</span>
          <span>AI statics</span>
          <span>50+ creatives / mo</span>
          <span>Data-driven</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works grid -->
    <section class="py-8">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-center mb-5">How Creative Testing Works</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5">
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F50D;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Research &amp; Script</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Analyze competitors, customer reviews, ad data. Write modular scripts with 3+ hooks per concept.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F3AC;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Produce &amp; Launch</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">UGC creators shoot, we edit. 40-70 videos per batch. Launch as ads within 2 weeks.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F4CA;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Measure &amp; Scale</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Tag every creative: Scale, Iterate, or Kill. Decisions from purchase data, not guesswork.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TOC -->
    <section class="py-10 border-t border-b border-border">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-muted-2 mb-4">Contents</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-1.5">
          {[
            { num: "01", text: "Overview", href: "#overview" },
            { num: "02", text: "What Is Creative Testing?", href: "#what" },
            { num: "03", text: "Why Most Brands Test Wrong", href: "#wrong" },
            { num: "04", text: "The System: How It Actually Works", href: "#system" },
            { num: "05", text: "Formats & Angles", href: "#formats" },
            { num: "06", text: "Creator Selection & Curation", href: "#creators" },
            { num: "07", text: "B-Roll & AI Production", href: "#broll" },
            { num: "08", text: "Metrics & Benchmarks", href: "#metrics" },
            { num: "09", text: "Economics", href: "#economics" },
            { num: "10", text: "Glossary", href: "#glossary" },
            { num: "11", text: "FAQ", href: "#faq" },
          ].map((item) => (
            <a href={item.href} class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[14px] text-ink-2 font-medium hover:bg-bg-alt transition-colors no-underline">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium text-accent min-w-[22px]">{item.num}</span>
              {item.text}
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 01 Overview -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="overview">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">01 &mdash; Overview</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Creative testing is volume &times; data</h2>
        <div class="bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.12)] rounded-xl p-5 mb-7">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">TL;DR</div>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Most brands produce 5-10 ads and guess which one is best</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Creative testing produces 40-70 per batch and lets purchase data decide</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">The winner rate in a well-run batch is ~30%. You need volume to hit it</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Traditional ad production is a creative bet: hire a team, produce a handful of polished videos, run them until they burn out. Creative testing flips this &mdash; produce many variations cheaply, run all of them, and let real purchase data tell you which ones work.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The model grew up inside DTC and tech companies spending $50K-$500K/month on paid media. At that spend level, the cost of a wrong creative is measured in tens of thousands of wasted dollars. The cost of testing 50 variations instead of 5 is trivial by comparison.</p>
        <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[100px]">Volume:</strong> 40-70 creatives per batch</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[100px]">Signal:</strong> real purchases, not views or likes</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[100px]">Cycle:</strong> 2-3 weeks per batch</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[100px]">Outcome:</strong> Scale winners, kill losers, iterate the middle</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 What Is Creative Testing -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="what">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">02 &mdash; Definition</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">What is creative testing?</h2>
        <div class="bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.12)] rounded-xl p-5 mb-7">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">TL;DR</div>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Producing many ad variations systematically, not one polished hero video</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Each variation tests one variable: hook, creator, format, angle, or CTA</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Winners are identified by CPA, not by likes or views</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Creative testing</strong> is a structured approach to paid ad production where every video is a hypothesis. Instead of producing one "best" ad, you produce dozens of variations &mdash; each testing a specific variable &mdash; and run all of them simultaneously as ads.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">A quick example</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A DTC supplement brand writes one script about bloating relief. From that script, they produce 12 videos: 3 different hooks &times; 2 creators &times; 2 formats (talking head vs voiceover + B-roll). All 12 run as ads. After $500 in spend, two have a CPA under $30 (target was $50). Those two get scaled. The other ten get killed or iterated. That's one creative test.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">What it is not</h3>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Not A/B testing a landing page</strong> &mdash; creative testing is about the ad itself, not where it sends traffic</li>
          <li><strong>Not brand video production</strong> &mdash; the goal is performance, not polish</li>
          <li><strong>Not influencer marketing</strong> &mdash; creators produce content for ads, not for their own audience</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 Why Most Brands Test Wrong -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="wrong">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">03 &mdash; The Problem</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Why most brands test wrong</h2>
        <div class="bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.12)] rounded-xl p-5 mb-7">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">TL;DR</div>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Too few creatives &mdash; 5-10 per month isn't enough data</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Testing too many variables at once</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Judging by views instead of purchases</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Most brands hire a videographer or agency to produce 5-10 ads per month. They pick the "best" one based on gut feeling, run it until it fatigues, and start over. This is not testing &mdash; it's guessing with expensive production.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The five mistakes</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step">Not enough volume &mdash; with a 30% winner rate, you need 30+ creatives to find 10 winners</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step">Changing too many variables at once &mdash; if the hook, creator, and format all change, you can't tell what worked</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step">Optimizing for views or CTR instead of CPA &mdash; a viral ad that doesn't convert is a cost center</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step">Not tracking creator-angle fit &mdash; the same script can cost $32/customer with one creator and $92 with another</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step">No system for iteration &mdash; winners aren't scaled, losers aren't analyzed</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 The System -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="system">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">04 &mdash; The System</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">How creative testing actually works</h2>
        <div class="bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.12)] rounded-xl p-5 mb-7">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">TL;DR</div>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Research &rarr; Scripts &rarr; Production &rarr; Data &rarr; Iterate</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Modular scripts: one body, multiple hooks and CTAs</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Every creative is tagged Scale / Iterate / Kill after 2-3 weeks of ad data</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The four stages</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Research.</strong> Analyze competitors' ads, your existing data, customer reviews. Build 5-8 testing angles &mdash; real pain points your customers have.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Scripts.</strong> Modular scripts: one proven body, multiple openings. 3 hooks &times; 2 creators &times; 2 formats = 12 videos from one concept.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Production.</strong> Creators shoot, we edit. UGC, voiceover + B-roll, AI statics, product demos. 40-70 videos in 2 weeks.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Data.</strong> After 2-3 weeks of ad data, tag every creative: Scale, Iterate, or Kill. Not likes &mdash; actual purchases.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Three batches, two months</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Batch 1: Find.</strong> 40-70 original videos testing multiple angles, creators, and formats. Every video is a hypothesis.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Batch 2: Scale.</strong> 10+ variations of every Batch 1 winner. New hooks, re-edited middles, different CTAs. Budget follows performance.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Batch 3: Find more.</strong> 50 new concepts, untested ideas, new pain points. Runs in parallel with Batch 2.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">By the end of month 2: 100-150 tested creatives, a clear picture of what works, and a system to keep finding winners.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Mid CTA -->
    <section class="py-10">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bg-dark rounded-2xl p-10 md:p-14 text-center">
          <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(22px,3.5vw,32px)] tracking-[-0.02em] text-white mb-3">Need creators or B-roll for your ads?</h2>
          <p class="text-[15px] text-muted max-w-[480px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-6">We handle creator curation, scripting, and B-roll production. You get tested creatives ready to run as ads.</p>
          <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap">
            <a href={emailCreators} class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-white text-ink hover:bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Order creator curation &rarr;</a>
            <a href={emailBroll} class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold text-muted border border-white/15 hover:text-white hover:border-white/30 transition-all no-underline">Order B-roll production &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 Formats & Angles -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="formats">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">05 &mdash; Formats</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Formats &amp; angles: the real edge</h2>
        <div class="bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.12)] rounded-xl p-5 mb-7">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">TL;DR</div>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">6 core formats: UGC talking head, VO + B-roll, before/after, product demo, POV, AI statics</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">In our data, VO + B-roll costs 25% less per customer than talking heads</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">You don't know which format wins until you test them all</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The six formats</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Format</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">What it is</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Best for</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">UGC talking head</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator speaks to camera</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Trust, authenticity</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">VO + B-roll</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Voiceover with product footage</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Lower CPA, visual products</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Before / After</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Transformation comparison</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Health, beauty, SaaS</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Product demo</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Screen recording or hands-on</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Tech, apps, AI tools</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">POV</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">First-person perspective</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Lifestyle, experience</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">AI statics</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">AI-generated images + motion</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Volume, visual variety</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Angles: 5-8 reasons people buy</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Each angle is a testing track. For supplements: bloating, fatigue, sleep. For AI products: speed, social proof, before/after. For fintech: hidden fees, instant transfers, rewards.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The hook library, angle library, and format library are the intellectual property of a creative testing program. Creators remix them into dozens of variants per week. Each variant is tracked back to its parent, so you know which hook families drive purchases.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 06 Creator Selection -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="creators">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">06 &mdash; Creators</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Creator selection &amp; curation</h2>
        <div class="bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.12)] rounded-xl p-5 mb-7">
          <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">TL;DR</div>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">The person matters more than the script</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Same script, different creator = 3x CPA difference</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">We test 2-3 creators per batch from a 600+ network</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">In our data, the same script can cost $32/customer with one creator and $92 with another. That 3x difference comes entirely from creator-product fit &mdash; how naturally they handle the product, how their energy matches the audience, how their face and voice build trust.</p>
